# Module 16's docker/dashboard.Dockerfile builds with `context: ../dashboard`
# (docker-compose.yml), not the repo root — Docker looks for .dockerignore
# INSIDE the build context directory, never the repo-root one, so that file's
# rules never applied here at all. Found the hard way: the dashboard build
# context was silently including node_modules/ (205 MB), turning a build that
# should transfer a few MB in a couple seconds into a 240+ second upload.

node_modules/
dist/
.git/
*.md
coverage/
.vscode/
.idea/
